#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:15
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:18
msgid ""
"ROS logging helps you monitor node behavior and diagnose problems by sending "
"logs to console output, log files, and the ``/rosout`` topic. This article "
"describes the available logging severities, APIs, configuration options, "
"environment, and implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:27
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:30
msgid "Logging and logger configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:32
msgid ""
"The logging subsystem in ROS 2 aims to deliver logging messages to a variety "
"of targets, including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:34
msgid "To the console (if one is attached)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:35
msgid "To log files on disk (if local storage is available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:36
msgid "To the ``/rosout`` topic on the ROS 2 network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:38
msgid ""
"By default, log messages in ROS 2 nodes will go out to the console (on "
"stderr), to log files on disk, and to the ``/rosout`` topic on the ROS 2 "
"network. All of the targets can be individually enabled or disabled on a per-"
"node basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:41
msgid ""
"The rest of this document will go over some of the ideas behind the logging "
"subsystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:44
msgid "Severity level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:46
msgid ""
"Log messages have a severity level associated with them: ``DEBUG``, "
"``INFO``, ``WARN``, ``ERROR`` or ``FATAL``, in ascending order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:48
msgid ""
"A logger will only process log messages with severity at or higher than a "
"specified level chosen for the logger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:50
msgid ""
"Each node has a logger associated with it that automatically includes the "
"node's name and namespace. If the node's name is externally remapped to "
"something other than what is defined in the source code, it will be "
"reflected in the logger name. Non-node loggers can also be created that use "
"a specific name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:54
msgid ""
"Logger names represent a hierarchy. If the level of a logger named "
"\"abc.def\" is unset, it will defer to the level of its parent named "
"\"abc\", and if that level is also unset, the default logger level will be "
"used. When the level of logger \"abc\" is changed, all of its descendants "
"(e.g. \"abc.def\", \"abc.ghi.jkl\") will have their level impacted unless "
"their level has been explicitly set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:59
msgid "APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:61
msgid ""
"These are the APIs that end users of the ROS 2 logging infrastructure should "
"use, split up by client library."
msgstr ""

