msgid ""
"``throttle_duration_sec`` - if not None, the duration of the throttle "
"interval in floating-point seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:94
msgid ""
"``skip_first`` - if True, output the message all but the first time this "
"line is hit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:95
msgid ""
"``once`` - if True, only output the message the first time this line is hit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:97
msgid ""
"``rclpy.logging.set_logger_level`` - Set the logging level for a particular "
"logger name to the given severity level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:98
msgid ""
"``rclpy.logging.get_logger_effective_level`` - Given a logger name, return "
"the logger level (which may be unset)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:101
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:103
msgid ""
"Since ``rclcpp`` and ``rclpy`` use the same underlying logging "
"infrastructure, the configuration options are the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:108
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:110
msgid ""
"The following environment variables control some aspects of the ROS 2 "
"loggers. For each of the environment settings, note that this is a process-"
"wide setting, so it applies to all nodes in that process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:113
msgid ""
"``RCL_LOGGING_IMPLEMENTATION`` - Control which logging backend "
"implementation to use at runtime (when using dynamic loading, which is the "
"default). If non-empty, use the specified logging implementation library "
"(e.g., ``rcl_logging_spdlog``, ``rcl_logging_noop``). If empty or not set, "
"defaults to ``rcl_logging_spdlog``. This variable has no effect when RCL is "
"built with static linking to a specific logging implementation. See the "
"``rcl_logging_implementation`` section below for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:118
msgid ""
"``RCL_LOGGING_SPDLOG_FLUSH_PERIOD_SECONDS`` - Control the periodic flush "
"interval for log files when using the ``rcl_logging_spdlog`` backend. By "
"default, logs are flushed every 5 seconds and immediately on error-level "
"messages. If set to ``0``, logs are flushed immediately on every log message "
"(unbuffered mode, which may impact performance). If set to a positive "
"integer ``N``, logs are flushed every ``N`` seconds plus immediately on "
"error-level messages. If set to an invalid value (non-integer, negative, or "
"trailing characters), initialization will fail with an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:123
msgid ""
"``ROS_LOG_DIR`` - Control the logging directory that is used for writing "
"logging messages to disk (if that is enabled). If non-empty, use the exact "
"directory as specified in this variable. If empty, use the contents of the "
"``ROS_HOME`` environment variable to construct a path of the form "
"``$ROS_HOME/.log``. In all cases, the ``~`` character is expanded to the "
"user's HOME directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:127
msgid ""
"``ROS_HOME`` - Control the home directory that is used for various ROS "
"files, including logging and config files. In the context of logging, this "
"variable is used to construct a path to a directory for log files. If non-"
"empty, use the contents of this variable for the ROS_HOME path. In all "
"cases, the ``~`` character is expanded to the users's HOME directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:131
msgid ""
"``RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT`` - Control what stream output messages go to. "
"If this is unset or 0, use stderr. If this is 1, use stdout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:134
msgid ""
"``RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM`` - Control whether the logging stream (as "
"configured in ``RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT``) should be line buffered or "
"unbuffered. If this is unset, use the default of the stream (generally line "
"buffered for stdout, and unbuffered for stderr). If this is 0, force the "
"stream to be unbuffered. If this is 1, force the stream to be line buffered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:138
msgid ""
"``RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT`` - Control whether colors are used when "
"outputting messages. If unset, automatically determine based on the platform "
"and whether the console is a TTY. If 0, force disable using colors for "
"output. If 1, force enable using colors for output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:142
msgid ""
"``RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT`` - Control the fields that are output for "
"each log message. The available fields are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:145
msgid "``{severity}`` - The severity level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:146
msgid "``{name}`` - The name of the logger (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:147
msgid "``{message}`` - The log message (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:148
msgid ""
"``{function_name}`` - The function name this was called from (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:149
msgid "``{file_name}`` - The file name this was called from (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:150
msgid ""
"``{short_file_name}`` - The file name without the directory path (basename "
"only) this was called from (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:151
msgid "``{time}`` - The time in seconds since the epoch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:152
msgid "``{time_as_nanoseconds}`` - The time in nanoseconds since the epoch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:153
msgid ""
"``{date_time_with_ms}`` - The time in ISO format, e.g. ``2024-06-11 "
"09:29:19.304``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:154
msgid ""
"``{line_number}`` - The line number this was called from (may be empty)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:156
msgid ""
"If no format is given, a default of ``[{severity}] [{time}] [{name}]: "
"{message}`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:158
msgid ""
"``RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT`` also supports the following escape "
"character syntax."
msgstr ""

