#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:177
msgid "Node creation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:179
msgid ""
"When initializing a ROS 2 node, it is possible to control some aspects of "
"the behavior via node options. Since these are per-node options, they can be "
"set differently for different nodes even when the nodes are composed into a "
"single process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:182
msgid ""
"``log_levels`` - The log level to use for a component within this particular "
"node. This can be set with the following: ``ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker --"
"ros-args --log-level talker:=DEBUG``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:184
msgid ""
"``external_log_config_file`` - The external file to use to configure the "
"backend logger. If it is NULL, the default configuration will be used. Note "
"that the format of this file is backend-specific (and is currently "
"unimplemented for the default backend logger of spdlog). This can be set "
"with the following: ``ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker --ros-args --log-config-"
"file log-config.txt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:188
msgid ""
"``log_stdout_disabled`` - Whether to disable writing log messages to the "
"console. This can be done with the following: ``ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp "
"talker --ros-args --disable-stdout-logs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:190
msgid ""
"``log_rosout_disabled`` - Whether to disable writing log messages out to ``/"
"rosout``. This can significantly save on network bandwidth, but external "
"observers will not be able to monitor logging. This can be done with the "
"following: ``ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker --ros-args --disable-rosout-"
"logs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:193
msgid ""
"``log_ext_lib_disabled`` - Whether to completely disable the use of an "
"external logger. This may be faster in some cases, but means that logs will "
"not be written to disk. This can be done with the following: ``ros2 run "
"demo_nodes_cpp talker --ros-args --disable-external-lib-logs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:198
msgid "Logging subsystem design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:200
msgid ""
"The image below shows the main pieces to the logging subsystem and how they "
"interact. Note that ``rcl`` can link to logging implementations either "
"through the ``rcl_logging_implementation`` abstraction layer (for runtime "
"dynamic loading, the default) or directly to a specific implementation like "
"``rcl_logging_spdlog`` (for static linking)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:203
msgid "ROS 2 logging architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:209
msgid "rcutils"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:211
msgid ""
"``rcutils`` has a logging implementation that can format log messages "
"according to a certain format (see ``Configuration`` above), and output "
"those log messages to a console. ``rcutils`` implements a complete logging "
"solution, but allows higher-level components to insert themselves into the "
"logging infrastructure in a dependency-injection model. This will become "
"more evident when we talk about the ``rcl`` layer below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:215
msgid ""
"Note that this is a *per-process* logging implementation, so anything that "
"is configured at this level will affect the entire process, not just "
"individual nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:218
msgid "rcl_logging_implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:220
msgid ""
"``rcl_logging_implementation`` is a package that enables runtime dynamic "
"loading of logging backends in ROS 2, similar to how ``rmw_implementation`` "
"works for middleware selection. This abstraction layer allows users to "
"switch between different logging implementations (such as "
"``rcl_logging_spdlog`` and ``rcl_logging_noop``) without rebuilding RCL or "
"application code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:223
msgid "rcl_logging_implementation architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:229
msgid "Runtime Dynamic Loading vs Static Linking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:231
msgid "The logging system supports two build configurations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:234
msgid "Dynamic Loading (Default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:236
msgid ""
"By default, ``rcl`` links against ``rcl_logging_implementation``, which "
"dynamically loads the logging backend at runtime. This approach provides "
"maximum flexibility, allowing the logging implementation to be changed via "
"environment variables without recompilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:239
msgid "When using dynamic loading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:241
msgid "The logging implementation is loaded as a shared library at runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:242
msgid ""
"The actual implementation can be selected via the "
"``RCL_LOGGING_IMPLEMENTATION`` environment variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:243
msgid "No rebuild is required to switch between logging implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:244
msgid ""
"All logging interface function symbols are resolved lazily when first "
"accessed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:247
msgid "Static Linking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:249
msgid ""
"For embedded systems or deployment scenarios requiring static linking, the "
"build system can be configured to link directly to a specific logging "
"implementation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:251
msgid ""
"Set the CMake variable ``RCL_LOGGING_IMPLEMENTATION`` at build time to "
"specify the implementation (e.g., ``rcl_logging_spdlog``, "
"``rcl_logging_noop``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:252
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set the ``RCL_LOGGING_IMPLEMENTATION`` environment variable "
"before running CMake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Logging/About-Logging.rst:253
msgid ""
"The specified implementation will be statically linked into the final "
"executable"
